          "suggestions": "The agent retrieved mean gas values via iot.sensor_stats for Transformer 1 at MAIN (window confirmed from first/last timestamps, 2024-01-15 to 2024-01-19), fetched the failure mode list via fmsr.get_failure_modes, and reported that fmsr.interpret_dga returned 'LLM unavailable' before computing the IEC 60599 ratios manually. The ratio values (C2H2/C2H4\u22480.0004, CH4/H2\u22482.56, C2H4/C2H6\u22483.05) and Duval Triangle 1 percentages (\u224830.6% CH4, 69.4% C2H4, 0.03% C2H2 \u2192 T3) are arithmetically correct from the retrieved means, the 10 ppm fallback was correctly checked and ruled out, the agreement between methods was explicitly assessed, and the failure mode 'Thermal Fault \u2014 Core/Winding' was drawn from the tool-provided list. Minor improvements: explicitly call iot.stream_extent to confirm the window as the expected behavior suggests, and consider retrying fmsr.interpret_dga (or noting the retry attempt) rather than relying solely on the manual fallback; the note about oti_a/oti_t flags was a reasonable inference from the retrieved data but could be more cautiously worded."
